WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.036
[ Crowd cheers ]
-3...2...1.

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:06.138
[ Imitates buzzer ]
That's it!

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:08.040
Good game, pal. I won.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.375
I don't know who you are,

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:10.709
but it was fun
playing against you.

00:00:10.709 --> 00:00:13.679
-You didn't win. I won.
-What?

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:15.215
-No, you didn't.
Look at the score.

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:17.784
-Stop the count.
-We did stop the count,

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:19.452
and I won.
-Keep counting.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:21.454
-I don't need to.
Look at the scoreboard.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:22.889
-We're demanding a recount,
folks.

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.991
Can you can believe this?
I'm being totally cheated.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.292
Everyone agrees.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.828
I'm in the process of suing
PlayStation right now.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.897
-What, uh -- President Trump?
-Fake news!

00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:34.767
-Oh, come on, just admit you
lost so we can all move on.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:36.569
Besides, don't you have
more important things to do

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:39.038
to be playing video games?
-I could ask you the same thing.

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:41.174
-It's time for the show.
I gotta go.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:46.112
-Hey, Dad, can I play?
-Get out of there, Eric!

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.414
-I'm Don Jr.

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:50.550
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:05.164
-From Rockefeller Center,

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:06.565
in the heart of
New York City,

00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:08.834
it's "The Tonight Show
Starring Jimmy Fallon."

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:10.436
Tonight, join Jimmy
and his guests --

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:13.473
Chance the Rapper,
Erin Andrews,

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:16.208
musical guests
G Herbo and Chance the Rapper --

00:01:16.208 --> 00:01:18.878
and featuring the legendary
Roots crew.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:21.948
And now here he is --
JimmyFallon!

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:24.150
-Do it!

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.920
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.256
Whoo!

00:01:31.256 --> 00:01:33.426
Hey! Thank you!

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.294
Hello, and welcome!

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:38.031
Thank you very much.
Please.

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:39.899
That is so nice.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.734
Oh, my goodness!

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.736
Oh, that's
what I'm talking about!

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.672
Thank you, thank you, thank you
very much.

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:47.840
Wow. What a crowd.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.275
You're not gonna believe this,

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:50.443
but the White House
just told me

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.378
we got a million people
in here tonight.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.847
Amazing, amazing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:57.583
Amazing.

00:01:57.583 --> 00:02:00.219
Well, let's get to
the news and jokes.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.454
Well, guys, as the pandemic
gets worse,

00:02:02.454 --> 00:02:04.457
President Trump is making it
even tougher

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.926
for President-Elect Biden
to deal with the crisis.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:08.594
Apparently, he's still not
letting

00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:11.430
his coronavirus task force
talk to Biden's.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:14.166
I'm really shocked by this,
'cause, up until now,

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:16.436
Trump's handling of the pandemic
has been flawless.

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:19.172
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.806
Seriously, why is it
so hard for Trump?

00:02:20.806 --> 00:02:22.808
He's been passing off COVID
responsibilities

00:02:22.808 --> 00:02:25.011
for eight months.
Why stop now?

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.512
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:28.981
I'm not surprised the transition
of power is taking so long.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:31.083
Every time Mike Pence hears
the word "transition,"

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:34.120
he runs and hides under the bed.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.657
"Mother, put on
'David and Goliath.'"

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:40.693
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:44.163
Not sure any of this matters.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:47.032
Trump's task force probably
wrote like one memo that says,

00:02:47.032 --> 00:02:49.202
"We think you get it
from licking stuff."

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.603
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:52.271
Honestly, do we even want
Trump's task force

00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:53.606
training Biden's?
That's like

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.975
getting legal advice
from Rudy Giuliani.

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:58.644
[ Laughter ]
"I'd like to represent myself."

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:01.014
[ Laughter ]
But here's some good news.

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.216
After last week's announcement
from Pfizer

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:05.584
that their vaccine is
more than 90% effective,

00:03:05.584 --> 00:03:07.653
another company, Moderna,

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:09.188
has made an announcement
of their own.

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:11.124 line:0%
Watch this.
-This morning, breaking news

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:12.858 line:0%
on the coronavirus vaccine.

00:03:12.858 --> 00:03:17.863 line:0%
Moderna announcing its vaccine
could be up to 94.5% effective.

00:03:17.863 --> 00:03:20.466
-That's an amazing achievement.
Scientists are like,

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.668
"We've harnessed
the power of mRNA,"

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:25.638
while Americans are like,
"Does it come in grape flavor?"

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:28.107
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:32.412
"Can I get it in the gummy shape
like Fred Flintstone?"

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:35.814
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.814 --> 00:03:37.650
I had to read that joke
as Brian Regan,

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.953
'cause it felt like --
it sounded like

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:42.388
Brian would have nailed that,
so that was for you, Brian.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:45.124
[ As Brian Regan ]
A gummy like --

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:47.393
like, Fred Flintstone
type of gummy.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:50.296
Bet I could do that.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:52.565
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.267
[ Normal voice ] Meanwhile,
this weekend in Washington,

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.869
Trump supporters gathered
to protest the election.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:59.338
And Trump even drove by
on his way to the golf course.

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:00.606 line:0%
Take a look.

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:03.041 line:0%
-Mr. Trump saluted a rally
from his motorcade

00:04:03.041 --> 00:04:06.212 line:0%
as thousands of Trump supporters
claimed election fraud.

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:08.448
-Yeah, nothing says
"Thanks for your support"

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:11.384
like barreling through the crowd
on your way to a golf course.

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:12.685
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:13.886
If you read his lips,
I think he's saying,

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:16.121
"They wasted a Saturday
for this?

00:04:16.121 --> 00:04:18.391
Could have gone golfing."

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:21.894
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:27.767
Can we show it again?
Just him going by his followers?

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:30.903 line:0%
-Mr. Trump saluted a rally
from his motorcade...

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:33.306
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, man.

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:36.075
And this was cute.

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:37.844
Trump's car -- I don't know
if you saw it --

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:39.378
even had a bunch of tin cans
hanging off the back

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:41.347
and a sign that said,
"Just Lost the Election."

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:43.582
I don't know.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:49.288
But Trump was overwhelmed
by the support.

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:50.789
And he was like,
"I love you guys.

00:04:50.789 --> 00:04:52.825
You're doing the white thing.
I mean, the right thing."

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.827
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:56.295
Well, if it's not clear by now,

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:58.564
Trump still isn't ready
to move on from the election.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:00.066
But yesterday,
for the first time,

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:03.201
it seemed like he was admitting
that Biden won.

00:05:03.201 --> 00:05:07.273
Trump tweeted, "He won because
the election was rigged."

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:10.743
Yep, that might be as close
to a concession speech

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:12.645
as we're gonna get, folks.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:15.581
But it was short-lived,
because he went on to say,

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:18.351
"I concede nothing,"
and, "I won the election."

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:20.286
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:22.454
Trump won't give up,
while the rest of us are like,

00:05:22.454 --> 00:05:25.591
"Dude, we've moved on
to Netflix shows about chess.

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:30.629
We -- We don't care.
We don't care, dude."

00:05:30.629 --> 00:05:32.198
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.266
Even though Trump's lawsuits
keep getting tossed out,

00:05:34.266 --> 00:05:36.502
it's clear the president
is not planning to concede

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.504
anytime soon.
So you know what?

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:41.107
We thought we'd do it for him
and give us

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:43.576
the concession speech
that we all deserve.

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:44.943
Take a look.

00:05:44.943 --> 00:05:47.613
[ "America the Beautiful"
plays ]

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:51.417
-My fellow Americans,
a short time ago,

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:53.585
Joe Biden beat me
in the election.

00:05:53.585 --> 00:05:57.356
And not only did he win,
he won by a lot, actually.

00:05:57.356 --> 00:05:59.959 line:0%
Therefore, it is time
for me to step aside.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:01.394
Because, let's face it,

00:06:01.394 --> 00:06:04.263
I wasn't probably on my game,
and I wasn't doing so well.

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:06.698
And you know, I'm the only
President in history

00:06:06.698 --> 00:06:10.636
to lose the popular vote twice
and to get impeached.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:12.571
It's time
for a change.

00:06:12.571 --> 00:06:15.875
The greatest dream in the world
is that Joe Biden wins,

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:19.345
because the winner of this vote
was decided

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:21.447
by a fair and open election.

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:25.651
Therefore, I humbly concede
to Joe Biden.

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:28.287
The American people
have responded.

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:30.322
And they have said to me,
"You're fired.

00:06:30.322 --> 00:06:31.824
Bing. Get out."

00:06:31.824 --> 00:06:33.592
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:33.592 --> 00:06:35.428
-[ Laughing ] Wow.

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:38.331
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.066 --> 00:06:43.735
Speaking of the election,
The Gap says

00:06:43.735 --> 00:06:46.305
sales of their pants
have nearly doubled

00:06:46.305 --> 00:06:48.107
since the election week,
and they think

00:06:48.107 --> 00:06:50.542
it has something to do
with Steve Kornacki.

00:06:50.542 --> 00:06:52.111
[ Laughter ]
Watch this.

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:53.745 line:0%
After many news outlets reported

00:06:53.745 --> 00:06:57.116 line:0%
that Kornacki's signature khakis
come from The Gap,

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:58.817 line:0%
the company reported it saw

00:06:58.817 --> 00:07:00.887 line:0%
a dramatic increase
in online traffic

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:06.024 line:0%
and a more than 90% sales
increase on khaki pants.

00:07:06.024 --> 00:07:08.060
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.896
Right now, Anna Wintour is like,

00:07:09.896 --> 00:07:12.664
"Why did I choose Harry Styles
for the cover of 'Vogue'?!"

00:07:12.664 --> 00:07:15.234
[ Laughter ]
"Kornacki!"

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:17.102
[ Laughter ]

00:07:17.102 --> 00:07:19.238
"I told you -- Kornacki!"

00:07:19.238 --> 00:07:20.906
[ Laughter ]

00:07:20.906 --> 00:07:22.474
Today, middle-aged white guys
were like,

00:07:22.474 --> 00:07:25.144
"Is this the line for the PS5s
or the Kornacki khakis?"

00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:27.212
[ Laughter ]

00:07:27.212 --> 00:07:28.947
Republicans don't know
how to feel right now.

00:07:28.947 --> 00:07:30.883
They lost the White House,
but khakis are back.

00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:33.286
[ Laughter ]
It's actually really impressive,

00:07:33.286 --> 00:07:35.121
because if there's one thing
Americans haven't been buying

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:37.356
during the pandemic, it's pants.

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:39.692
[ Laughter ]
Some more business news.

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:42.494
Costco is now offering
its members a new service.

00:07:42.494 --> 00:07:43.662
Listen to this.

00:07:43.662 --> 00:07:45.797 line:0%
-There's a new membership option
at Costco.

00:07:45.797 --> 00:07:48.901 line:0%
Private jet company Wheels Up
has partnered with the retailer

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:51.103 line:0%
to offer 12-month memberships
for its service,

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:55.374 line:0%
starting at the low, low price
of $17,500.

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:59.411
-As if someone is gonna be
shopping like, "Okay,

00:07:59.411 --> 00:08:02.048
I got the whole chicken,
I got a box of Go-Gurt,

00:08:02.048 --> 00:08:04.983
uh, toilet paper,
and, oh, I almost forgot,

00:08:04.983 --> 00:08:07.386
I need that, uh,
jet membership."

00:08:07.386 --> 00:08:10.356
[ Laughter ]

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:12.959
[ Chuckles ]

00:08:12.959 --> 00:08:15.561
Can I try reading it
as Brian Regan again?

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:17.563
[ Laughter ]

00:08:17.563 --> 00:08:19.064
[ As Brian Regan ] Let's see,
I got the whole chicken,

00:08:19.064 --> 00:08:22.768
got a box of Go-Gurt,
I got the toilet paper.

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:26.839
Uh, almost forgot, I need
that jet membership!

00:08:26.839 --> 00:08:28.707
[ Normal voice ] Nah,
that's not it.

00:08:28.707 --> 00:08:31.076
[ Applause ]
It's not working as good.

00:08:31.076 --> 00:08:32.978
This is cool, though.

00:08:32.978 --> 00:08:34.946
Since it's Costco, they
come around midflight

00:08:34.946 --> 00:08:36.882
and offer everyone
a 10-gallon drum of peanuts.

00:08:36.882 --> 00:08:38.451
I thought that was good.

00:08:38.451 --> 00:08:40.219
Hey, guys,
Thanksgiving is next week,

00:08:40.219 --> 00:08:42.288
And I saw that Baskin-Robbins
has brought back

00:08:42.288 --> 00:08:44.457
its turkey ice cream cake.
Take a look.

00:08:44.457 --> 00:08:46.658
There it is.

00:08:46.658 --> 00:08:48.727
Because all kids were like,
"If only our favorite treat

00:08:48.727 --> 00:08:50.629
looked more like
a dead bird carcass.

00:08:50.629 --> 00:08:52.531
Unh!"
[ Laughter ]

00:08:52.531 --> 00:08:53.666
What is that?
It looks like

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:55.501
they spray-painted
Thor's helmet.

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:57.903
[ Laughter ]

00:08:57.903 --> 00:08:59.438
Not to be outdone, Cinnabon

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:01.740
just started selling
its frosting by the pint.

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:03.743
Look at this. Wow.

00:09:03.743 --> 00:09:06.045
That's right, it's all the fun
of eating Cinnabon

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:08.514
with double the depression.

00:09:08.514 --> 00:09:11.917
It's perfect for anyone looking
to Flex Seal their arteries.

00:09:11.917 --> 00:09:14.286
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.286 --> 00:09:16.488
Actually, this is great.

00:09:16.488 --> 00:09:19.025
Now I have something to baste
the Baskin-Robbins turkey with.

00:09:19.025 --> 00:09:20.425
[ Laughter ]

00:09:20.425 --> 00:09:22.261
Here's a crazy story
from overseas.

00:09:22.261 --> 00:09:24.563
A school in France
had to ask parents

00:09:24.563 --> 00:09:27.833
to stop throwing their kids over
the 6-foot gate

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:30.002
when they showed up late
for school.

00:09:30.002 --> 00:09:32.104 line:0%
Check out the sign that they
actually had to hang up.

00:09:32.104 --> 00:09:35.106 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:09:35.106 --> 00:09:36.475
Yeah, it's dangerous.

00:09:36.475 --> 00:09:38.410
Apparently,
while landing on the other side,

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:40.646
some kids broke
their wine bottle.

00:09:40.646 --> 00:09:43.749
[ French accent ] Now what will
I pair with my Lunchables?

00:09:43.749 --> 00:09:47.019
[ Laughter ]

00:09:47.019 --> 00:09:48.521
[ Normal voice ] Meanwhile,
the parents

00:09:48.521 --> 00:09:50.422
are already one step ahead.

00:09:50.422 --> 00:09:51.690
Now they're taking
stale baguettes

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:54.260
and making their kids
pole-vault over the fence.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.428
[ Laughter ]

00:09:56.428 --> 00:10:01.400
[ Chuckling ]

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.002
And finally, a scuba diver
off the coast of Egypt

00:10:04.002 --> 00:10:06.272
just set an amazing new record.
Take a look at this.

00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:09.608 line:0%
-An Egyptian scuba diver has
broken a new world record.

00:10:09.608 --> 00:10:14.180 line:0%
He spent 145 hours, or almost
six whole days, underwater.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:15.547
-Wow. Yeah.

00:10:15.547 --> 00:10:17.382
Yeah, he came up,
learned it was still 2020,

00:10:17.382 --> 00:10:18.717
and went back down.

00:10:18.717 --> 00:10:21.020
Well, guys,
here's some fun news.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:23.689
Last night, we won
a People's Choice Award!

00:10:23.689 --> 00:10:27.125
Yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:27.125 --> 00:10:30.429
We won for Nighttime Talk Show
of 2020.

00:10:30.429 --> 00:10:31.930
It's so cool.

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:33.432
I just want to thank the
People's Choice Awards.

00:10:33.432 --> 00:10:36.102
And thank you to everyone
who voted for us.

00:10:36.102 --> 00:10:37.803
This award is always special

00:10:37.803 --> 00:10:40.172
because it comes from you,
the people.

00:10:40.172 --> 00:10:42.675
We try to put on the best show
we can for you guys every night,

00:10:42.675 --> 00:10:44.410
and it's a real honor
to be awarded.

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:46.178
So thank you so much again
for that.

00:10:46.178 --> 00:10:48.614
[ Cheers and applause ]
It's cool.

00:10:48.614 --> 00:10:50.416
I'll pass it around.

00:10:50.416 --> 00:10:52.718
Everyone gets it for a weekend,
yeah.

00:10:52.718 --> 00:10:54.453
-Okay, cool. Cool.

00:10:54.453 --> 00:10:57.222
-Guys, it's Monday.
We're excited to be back.

00:10:57.222 --> 00:10:58.924
We have a great week of shows
coming up.

